IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pbha-holidays`
IMPORT `pbha-qa`

-- Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (pbha-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role
-- and every situation.
--
-- 1. For the roles a question is about: the answer, worked by hand from the deposited text (weekdays from 1 January of each
--    year, as in the baseline's cases), and for the employee (the baseline's seat) the answer the baseline export gives on
--    the same facts, wrapped in the answer type.
-- 2. For each role a question is not about: every other input an ASSUMEd value, and the answer `does not arise for you`.
--    Reading an ASSUMEd BOOLEAN, NUMBER or DATE, or CONSIDERing an ASSUMEd Holiday (the baseline lists every value), stops
--    the evaluation, so these cases show the form need not ask those inputs.
-- 3. For each situation input, for the value under which it does not hold (FALSE for both): the inputs after it ASSUMEd,
--    and the answer `does not arise for you`.
--
-- Parts 2 and 3 were generated by the scratch script gen_dna.py; part 1 was written by hand. The Sovereign's birthday is an
-- input; 23 September 2024, 26 September 2022 and 28 September 2026 are the baseline's dates (the encoder's understanding of
-- the proclaimed days, not read in the deposit); 28 September elsewhere is a neutral placeholder.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

`as the employee` MEANS `I work in Western Australia`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ people in Western Australia`
`as the bank` MEANS `I run a bank, or a bank branch, in Western Australia`

§§ `Everyone: the calendar`

-- chloe c042 (2024): Easter, Labour Day, Western Australia Day, the King's Birthday; no weekend extra days.
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the employee` `Good Friday` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the holiday` (`falls on` (Date 29 3 2024))
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the employee` `Labour Day` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the holiday` (`falls on` (Date 4 3 2024))
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the employee` `the Monday after New Year's Day` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the holiday` `does not arise this year`
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the employee` `Western Australia Day` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the holiday` (`On what day does this holiday fall` `Western Australia Day` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024))
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the employer` `Australia Day` 2020 (Date 28 9 2020) EQUALS `the holiday` (`falls on` (Date 27 1 2020))
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the employer` `the Tuesday after Boxing Day` 2022 (Date 26 9 2022) EQUALS `the holiday` (`falls on` (Date 27 12 2022))
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the bank` `the Monday after Boxing Day` 2026 (Date 28 9 2026) EQUALS `the holiday` (`falls on` (Date 28 12 2026))
#ASSERT `On what day does this public holiday fall in WA` `as the bank` `Labour Day` 2027 (Date 28 9 2027) EQUALS `the holiday` (`falls on` (Date 1 3 2027))

-- c042: Chloe's 2024 -- eleven days, none doubled; 2021, fourteen; 2026, thirteen.
#ASSERT `What are the public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employee` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the days` (LIST (Date 1 1 2024), (Date 26 1 2024), (Date 4 3 2024), (Date 29 3 2024), (Date 31 3 2024), (Date 1 4 2024), (Date 25 4 2024), (Date 3 6 2024), (Date 23 9 2024), (Date 25 12 2024), (Date 26 12 2024))
#ASSERT `What are the public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employee` 2022 (Date 26 9 2022) EQUALS `the days` (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` 2022 (Date 26 9 2022))
#ASSERT `What are the public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employer` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the days` (LIST (Date 1 1 2024), (Date 26 1 2024), (Date 4 3 2024), (Date 29 3 2024), (Date 31 3 2024), (Date 1 4 2024), (Date 25 4 2024), (Date 3 6 2024), (Date 23 9 2024), (Date 25 12 2024), (Date 26 12 2024))
#ASSERT `What are the public holidays in WA in this year` `as the bank` 2026 (Date 28 9 2026) EQUALS `the days` (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` 2026 (Date 28 9 2026))
#ASSERT `How many days are public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employee` 2024 (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `count` 11
#ASSERT `How many days are public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employee` 2021 (Date 28 9 2021) EQUALS `count` 14
#ASSERT `How many days are public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employee` 2026 (Date 28 9 2026) EQUALS `count` (`How many public holidays in WA this year` 2026 (Date 28 9 2026))
#ASSERT `How many days are public holidays in WA in this year` `as the employer` 2026 (Date 28 9 2026) EQUALS `count` 13
#ASSERT `How many days are public holidays in WA in this year` `as the bank` 2022 (Date 26 9 2022) EQUALS `count` 13

-- Two Schedule days on one date: one day off.
#ASSERT `Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA` `as the employee` (Date 25 4 2011) (Date 28 9 2011) EQUALS `the holidays` (LIST `Easter Monday`, `Anzac Day`)
#ASSERT `Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA` `as the employee` (Date 26 12 2022) (Date 26 9 2022) EQUALS `the holidays` (`Which holidays fall on this day` (Date 26 12 2022) (Date 26 9 2022))
#ASSERT `Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA` `as the employer` (Date 26 4 2038) (Date 28 9 2038) EQUALS `the holidays` (LIST `Easter Monday`, `the Monday after Anzac Day`)
#ASSERT `Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA` `as the bank` (Date 6 5 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `the holidays` EMPTY

-- ss 5, 6: every Saturday, and every Schedule day.
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the employee` (Date 6 1 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the employee` (Date 4 3 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the employee` (Date 6 5 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the employee` (Date 7 5 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this day a bank holiday in WA` (Date 7 5 2024) (Date 23 9 2024))
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the employer` (Date 25 12 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the bank` (Date 6 1 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this day a bank holiday in Western Australia` `as the bank` (Date 8 1 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS no

§§ `The employee and the employer`

-- c042: Chloe's Labour Day and Western Australia Day, an ordinary Monday, Australia Day 2020 moved off the Sunday, and the
-- baseline's proclamations (the encoder's illustrations).
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employee` (Date 4 3 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `public holiday` `yes: a public holiday under s 5 and the Second Schedule`
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employee` (Date 6 5 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `public holiday` `no: not a public holiday in WA`
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employee` (Date 26 1 2020) (Date 28 9 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `public holiday` `no: not a public holiday in WA`
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employee` (Date 22 9 2022) (Date 26 9 2022) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `public holiday` `yes: a special public holiday by proclamation under s 7`
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employee` (Date 3 6 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `public holiday` (`Is this day a public holiday for me in WA` (Date 3 6 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employer` (Date 26 4 2011) (Date 28 9 2011) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `public holiday` `yes: a public holiday instead of a Schedule day, by proclamation under s 8`
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employer` (Date 3 6 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `public holiday` `no: the Governor has moved this day's holiday to another day under s 8`
#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the employer` (Date 27 1 2020) (Date 28 9 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `public holiday` `yes: a public holiday under s 5 and the Second Schedule`

-- ss 3, 9, with a WA instrument.
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `prevails` `this Act: a substitute day for Easter Sunday because it falls on a weekend has no effect (s 3(3))`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `prevails` `no inconsistency: both apply`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `prevails` `the proclamation (s 9)`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `prevails` (`Does my award or this Act prevail` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `prevails` `my industrial instrument (s 3(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `prevails` `the proclamation (s 9)`
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the employee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does my award's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the employer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes

§§ `s 10 -- banks`

-- A Saturday that is a bank holiday only by s 6 (6 January 2024): no need to close; Christmas Day 2021, a Saturday: close.
#ASSERT `Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` `as the employee` TRUE (Date 6 1 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` `as the employee` TRUE (Date 25 12 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` `as the employee` TRUE (Date 23 9 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS `yes if` (`Must my bank close to the public on this day` (Date 23 9 2024) (Date 23 9 2024))
#ASSERT `Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` `as the bank` (Date 6 1 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` `as the bank` (Date 25 12 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` `as the bank` (Date 27 12 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` `as the bank` (Date 7 5 2024) (Date 23 9 2024) EQUALS no

-- ASSUMEd inputs: reading any of them stops the evaluation, so a case that passes with them shows they were not read.
ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked Holiday` IS A Holiday

§§ `Each question, asked for every role it is not about: does not arise, and nothing else is read`

#ASSERT `Is this day a public holiday where the work is done` `as the bank` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the bank` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the bank` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` `as the employer` `an unasked fact` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` `as the bank` `an unasked fact` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` `as the employee` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must I close my bank's premises to the public on this day` `as the employer` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§ `Each situation input, for each value under which it does not hold: does not arise, and nothing after it is read`

-- `a WA industrial instrument covers the work`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employee` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the industrial instrument or the Act prevail on public holidays` `as the employer` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the employee` FALSE `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the instrument's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` `as the employer` FALSE `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- `I work in a bank`
#ASSERT `Must the bank where I work close to the public on this day` `as the employee` FALSE `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

